 "notes": "36 stations printed, lines 1518-1553, one line each, in a single column (station + type, then keepers). The list has no sub-headings, so coast is the section heading as printed (\"EAST COAST OF ENGLAND.\" without the full stop). Fragments are the whole printed lines, including the two-space indent and the padding between columns. The full stop that ends each keepers entry is left out of the keepers values. It is kept in fragments, and inside _Nil._ in other.\n\nNo map numbers, return marks (*, † etc.) or light characters are printed in this list. So number, marks and character are null throughout.\n\nCount mismatch: the paragraph just above (lines 1510-1511) says schedules went to forty-five stations and returns came from forty-two. The list has 36 rows, and four of them are _Nil._ (Spurn L.V., Hasbro' L.H., Nore L.V., Varne L.V.), which leaves 32 with keepers. Either the list is incomplete or the counts include stations not named here. Check against the other years.\n\nSpellings copied as printed, possibly odd:\n- \"Llyn Wells\" (presumably Lynn Well L.V.)\n- \"Languard Point\" (Landguard Point)\n- \"Hasbro'\" (Haisborough/Happisburgh), printed this way for both the L.V. and the L.H.\n- \"Farn, Inner,\" (Inner Farne)\n- \"Orfordness\" as one word\n- \"Newarp\" and \"Charles Perfrement\" are as printed\n- \"I. H. Johnson\": the I may be a J misprinted or OCR'd as I\n\n\"Tees, 5 Buoy\": \"5 Buoy\" is part of the light-vessel's name (the vessel at the No. 5 buoy), not a map number, so number is null.\n\n\"Whitby High\" keeps \"High\" in the name (the High light at Whitby).\n\nHanois is a Guernsey (Channel Islands) light, not on the East Coast. It is listed under this heading anyway; nothing in the row says where it is, so place is null.\n\nSpurn and Hasbro' each have two rows, an L.H. and an L.V. These are separate stations.\n\nLines 1555 onward (\"Reports and notes have also been received from:--\") list private observers, not stations, and are not included.",
